<title>HUNGARY: Hungary June CPI up 1.7 pct, 18.7 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Hungary June CPI up 1.7 pct, 18.7 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's consumer prices rose 1.7 percent in June month-on-month, taking the year-on-year figure to 18.7 percent, the Central Statistical Office said in a statement on Friday.  </p>
<p>DETAILED DATA FOR JUNE 1997</p>
<p>							    Weight in</p>
<p>				mth/mth   yr/yr	   index (pct)</p>
<p> Food products		4.0     20.8	     28.6</p>
<p>Alcoholic</p>
<p>beverages and</p>
<p> tobacco products	   1.0     18.7		9.0</p>
<p> Clothing		     0.7     18.4		6.3</p>
<p> Durable consumer goods   0.5	7.8		6.2</p>
<p> Household energy	   1.3     26.3		8.0</p>
<p> Other goods, fuels	 0.7     14.9	     17.0</p>
<p> Services		     0.9     18.6	     24.9</p>
<p> Total			  1.7     18.7	    100.0</p>
<p>NOTE - The CPI was boosted by government measures by 0.1 percent within the total 1.7 percent month-on-month rise in June, the KSH said. It added that the 4.0 percent rise in food prices was due to the seasonality of fruit and vegetable prices.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
